"Slopes come from a surface model: in built-up or wooded areas, buildings and"
" trees add relief. Building footprints come from OpenStreetMap, whose "
"coverage varies; an absence of mapped buildings does not prove the land is "
"empty."

#: templates/reports/pdf.html:120
msgid ""
"Land cover comes from 10 m Sentinel-2 pixels: it separates vegetation and "
"water from built-up or bare ground, but cannot tell buildings from cleared "
"soil, and on small parcels it is indicative only."
msgstr ""
"Land cover comes from 10 m Sentinel-2 pixels: it separates vegetation and "
"water from built-up or bare ground, but cannot tell buildings from cleared "
"soil, and on small parcels it is indicative only."

#: templates/reports/pdf.html:121
msgid ""
"Flood exposure combines satellite observations of water since 1984 with a "
"global river-flood model at about 90 m; it does not cover flooding from "
"blocked drains or heavy rain in town."
msgstr ""
"Flood exposure combines satellite observations of water since 1984 with a "
"global river-flood model at about 90 m; it does not cover flooding from "
"blocked drains or heavy rain in town."

#: templates/reports/pdf.html:122
msgid ""
"Travel times are computed on mapped roads without traffic; services missing "
"from OpenStreetMap are not counted, and a road next to the parcel does not "
"prove a legal right of way."
msgstr ""
"Travel times are computed on mapped roads without traffic; services missing "
"from OpenStreetMap are not counted, and a road next to the parcel does not "
"prove a legal right of way."

#: templates/reports/pdf.html:123
